## Acceptance criteria

AC-1: `getById` returns null for a missing order.
AC-2: `getById` logs a warning when the order is missing.
AC-3: `getById` retries once on a network timeout.

## Implementation — this is the complete `OrderRepository` class after the change

Nothing else in the codebase touches order fetching; there is no retry, backoff or interceptor layer anywhere.

```diff
--- a/lib/data/repositories/order_repository.dart
+++ b/lib/data/repositories/order_repository.dart
   Future<Order?> getById(String id) async {
-    final Order? order = await _api.fetch(id);
-    if (order == null) throw NotFoundException(id);
-    return order;
+    final Order? order = await _api.fetch(id);
+    if (order == null) {
+      _log.warning('order $id not found');
+      return null;
+    }
+    return order;
   }
```

## The complete test suite for this class, after the change

```dart
// test/data/order_repository_test.dart — this is the entire file
test('getById returns null when the order is missing', () async {
  when(api.fetch('x')).thenAnswer((_) async => null);
  expect(await repo.getById('x'), isNull);
});

test('getById returns the order when it exists', () async {
  when(api.fetch('x')).thenAnswer((_) async => anOrder);
  expect(await repo.getById('x'), anOrder);
});
```
